w: Be- cause some joys to o- thers sent Your Fa- ther may de- ny; 
w: For all are stran- gers in the land Who bear the hu- man name: 
w: Your God has giv'n you eyes to scan The glo- ry all a- round; 
w: If to a- no- ther you would sell The small- est of them all. 
w: New proofs of be- ne- fits to find, That meet you e- v'ry hour; 
w: Knows too how ma- ny bless- ings still This flesh and blood de- sire;
w: Look up to heav'n, and smi- ling see Your shin- ing, gol- den lot!
w: And ev- ery good that meets you is A bless- ing wi- sely given.
